# ============================================================
# plan: shutdown -- at air with everything off, from wherever the chamber is
# ============================================================
# The one plan to run after any End, and at the end of a session. In order: the
# cooler's, the article's and the camera's supplies off; both zones set to 25 °C
# and turned on, so they move toward the vent window while the pumps stop; the
# chamber sealed from the turbo and every pump stopped (seal chamber: the turbo
# gets turbo_spindown_s to stop turning, backed meanwhile); air let in once both
# zones are between 10 and 60 °C; both zones off. Every step reads first, so from
# a chamber already at rest or at air it changes little and ends in minutes.
#
# Start: any state, with no run going (End first) and no controller fault.
# End:   at atmosphere, the vent valve open, every other valve closed, both pumps
#   off, both zones off with their setpoints at 25 °C, psu1 CH1 and CH2 and psu2
#   CH1 off. The door may be opened.
# Fails: a controller fault (clear it at the HMI, then run it again); a zone not
#   between 10 and 60 °C within 4 hours (cooling from above 60 °C needs liquid
#   nitrogen); the chamber not above 700 Torr within 10 minutes. Wherever it
#   stops, End runs: the chamber stays sealed, the zones go off.
#
# Takes minutes from a rest; up to 4 hours from -150 °C at 1 °C/min. The zones'
# ramp rates are left as the last test set them: an article may still be inside.

load rLACO rPSU
record every 5 s

psu1 ch1 off
psu1 ch2 off
psu2 ch1 off
hvc platen 25
hvc shroud 25
hvc platen on
hvc shroud on
seal chamber
vent within 240 min
hvc platen off
hvc shroud off
log at atmosphere, every pump, zone and supply off; the door may be opened
